    <item>
      <title>MP1: Marketing surface (tools hub, methodology pages, cookie preferences, changelog)</title>
      <link>https://crowagent.ai/changelog#mp1-marketing-surface</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">crowagent-changelog-2026-05-05-mp1-marketing-surface</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 05 May 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <!-- TM-REMEDIATION-001 (2026-07-28): trailing clause "and a banned-phrase
           cleanup pass on the CrowCash product page" removed. The entry's subject is
           the tools hub; the clause was an incidental mention of a parked product. -->
      <description>New /tools hub aggregating six free regulator-grade tools, six SEO landing pages, six long-form methodology pages, /cookie-preferences with three-category consent model, /changelog with RSS endpoint, and top nav and footer extended with a Free Tools surface.</description>
    </item>

    <!-- TM-REMEDIATION-001 (2026-07-28): the "Phase 2 launch: CrowCyber and CrowCash"
         entry was REMOVED from this feed, not rewritten.
         Its description contained "CrowCash AI credit control and accounts
         receivable" - the closest wording anywhere on this site to the opposing
         mark's actual services (Crowe is an audit, tax and advisory network).
         On the honesty question: a changelog is a factual record, and rewriting an
         entry to describe something that did not ship would be a lie. Declining to
         keep PUBLISHING an entry about products we no longer offer publicly is not.
         So the entry is deleted rather than reworded, and the shipped history
         remains in git and in the tm-baseline-2026-07-28 tag. -->

    <item>
      <title>Cloudflare Pages migration complete</title>
      <link>https://crowagent.ai/changelog#cloudflare-pages-migration</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">crowagent-changelog-2026-04-26-cloudflare-pages-migration</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 26 Apr 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <description>crowagent.ai now serves from Cloudflare Pages (project crowagent-website). app.crowagent.ai and portal.crowagent.ai remain on Vercel. Eliminated cross-repo Vercel deployment risk.</description>
    </item>

